{
  "cell": "xor2",
  "_comment": [
    "Cell descriptor for layout/bin/compose-cell.py -- see layout/README.md",
    "section 'Composing a gate' for the floorplan reasoning shared with every",
    "other cell, and layout/xor2/README.md for this cell's own result and for",
    "why it needs neither a third routing plane nor a channel router, both of",
    "which layout/xor2-placement-poc/ predicted it would.",
    "",
    "xor2 is design/ro_array_core.spice's combining-tree XOR: two inverters",
    "(a->an, b->bn) feeding a static-CMOS XOR network -- a PMOS pull-up tree",
    "(Mp1||Mp2 from vdd to mid, Mp3||Mp4 from mid to y) and an NMOS pull-down",
    "tree (Mn1-Mn2 and Mn3-Mn4, two series pairs from y to vss). Twelve",
    "devices, ten nets. Three structural moves collapse that into SIX placed",
    "blocks plus three taps, and the whole cell into two gen-compose stages:",
    "",
    "1. READ THE PULL-UP TREE AS TWO SERIES CHAINS, NOT TWO PARALLEL PAIRS.",
    "   vdd -[Mp1,g=a]- mid -[Mp3,g=an]- y and vdd -[Mp2,g=b]- mid -[Mp4,",
    "   g=bn]- y are each a two-transistor series chain, so each is ONE",
    "   mos_array call with fingers=2, finger_topology='series' (ports",
    "   U0_S0/U0_G0/U0_D0/U0_G1/U0_S1). The two chains share `mid`, which is",
    "   each chain's INTERIOR U0_D0 segment -- reported and contactable, so",
    "   the shared node is a single 2-pin route rather than a 4-pin bundle.",
    "   ro_nand2 already used a series pair (mnab) but left its U0_D0",
    "   deliberately unconnected; this is the first cell here to wire one.",
    "   The pull-down tree is the same shape (mn12, mn34), and there BOTH",
    "   interior nodes (s1, s2) stay unwired exactly as ro_nand2's did.",
    "2. THE TWO INVERTERS ARE ro_buf. XMpiA/XMniA and XMpiB/XMniB are",
    "   byte-for-byte ro_buf's own device pair (pfet 0.84/0.15 + nfet",
    "   0.42/0.15, out/in/vdd/vss), so each is placed as an already-composed",
    "   blocks[].cell -- ro_ring5's technique, applied to a leaf gate instead",
    "   of a ring. Its `a` and `y` ports are hand-declared on ro_buf's own",
    "   internal li1 wires: `a` at local (0.545, 1.70) exits WEST through the",
    "   free band between ro_buf's mn (top edge 1.24) and mp (bottom edge",
    "   2.14); `y` at local (1.90, 1.20) exits EAST on the x=1.90 leg of",
    "   ro_buf's own y route, clear of both device bboxes (mn x1=1.09, mp",
    "   x1=1.24). The two exit in OPPOSITE directions, which is what lets",
    "   inv_a feed the west columns and inv_b the east ones.",
    "3. SPLIT THE NETS BY LAYER, NOT BY LANE. Stage 'core' routes vdd, mid, y",
    "   and vss on li1 -- attic (y=14.4/15.0) for mid/vdd, one li1 lane at",
    "   y=4.6 across the channel for y, basement (y=2.0) for vss -- and",
    "   promotes all eight gate pads plus the four inverter signal ports as",
    "   bare pins. The final stage routes a/an/b/bn on metal2 (met1) over",
    "   that composed cell. The gate nets therefore share the channel with",
    "   nothing, and the supply/output nets share the attic and basement with",
    "   nothing: the two groups cross each other freely because they are on",
    "   different layers, which is what removes the congestion the",
    "   placement-only PoC hit.",
    "",
    "Column order (chosen so that only two of the four gate nets are long):",
    "mp13 is mirror_y and mp24 is rotate_180, so the top row reads",
    "vdd,a,mid,an,y | y,bn,mid,b,vdd -- the two `y` pads face each other",
    "across the top gap (one straight li1 route) and the two `vdd` pads land",
    "at the two outer ends (one attic run). The NMOS row has no such freedom",
    "(an nfet's gates only face up in orientation 'none'), so mn34/mn12 read",
    "y,an,s2,bn,vss | y,a,s1,b,vss. The resulting gate columns are",
    "a(0.545)/an(1.215)/bn(7.695)/b(8.365) on top and",
    "an(0.895)/bn(1.565)/a(7.895)/b(8.565) on the bottom, which makes `an`",
    "and `b` adjacent local pairs and leaves exactly two nets spanning the",
    "cell: `a` west-to-east and `bn` east-to-west. Those two would cross in",
    "the channel, so `a` takes the met1 basement (y=1.0) and `bn` the met1",
    "attic (y=16.0) -- opposite sides of the cell, no crossing, and no third",
    "routing plane needed."
  ],
  "pdk": {
